  "line": "Edom was a rugged, mountainous land south of the Dead Sea, home to Israel's \"brother\" nation, and a place of refusal, war, and rebellion against Israel and Judah.",
  "moments": [
    {
      "title": "Edom Says No to Israel",
      "text": "Moses sent messengers asking the king of Edom to let Israel pass along the King's Highway. Edom refused and came out with a large army, so Israel turned away.",
      "passage": "Numbers 20:14-21"
    },
    {
      "title": "David Rules Edom",
      "text": "David struck down eighteen thousand Edomites in the Valley of Salt. He put soldiers throughout Edom, and all the Edomites came under his rule.",
      "passage": "2 Samuel 8:12-14"
    },
    {
      "title": "Joab Strikes Edom",
      "text": "When David was in Edom, his army commander Joab stayed six months and killed every male there. Years later, the LORD raised up Hadad the Edomite, a young boy who had escaped to Egypt, as an enemy against Solomon.",
      "passage": "1 Kings 11:14-22"
    },
    {
      "title": "Water Flows from Edom",
      "text": "Three kings took a route by way of the Desert of Edom and ran out of water. After Elisha spoke the LORD's word, water flowed from the direction of Edom the next morning and filled the land.",
      "passage": "2 Kings 3:8-20"
    },
    {
      "title": "Edom Rebels Against Judah",
      "text": "In the days of Jehoram, Edom rebelled against Judah and chose its own king. The writer says Edom has been in rebellion to this day.",
      "passage": "2 Kings 8:20-22"
    }
  ],
